How does MetricPoller.send() work?

Code signature: public send(Map<String, JsonObject> contexts, String errorCode, String error) { ... }
File: src/main/java/com/mindarray/nms/MetricPoller.java

results.model_output:
s method iterates through a map of contexts and processes each one with the extract method,
which formats the error information and sends it. After processing each context, it removes
it from the map to free up memory and prevent duplicate processing.

The method determines the appropriate error message based on the error code:
- For PROCESS_TIMEOUT errors: Uses the PROCESS_TIMED_OUT message
- For other errors: Uses the INTERNAL_ERROR message

@code
public void send(Map<String, JsonObject> contexts, String errorCode, String error)
{
    if (!contexts.isEmpty())
    {
        for (var entry : contexts.entrySet())
        {
            var id = entry.getKey();

            var context = entry.getValue();

            var targetIp = context.getString(MetricContextConstants.TARGET_IP);

            if (error != null && !error.isEmpty())
            {
                LOGGER.warn(String.format("Error occurred for %s with message %s", targetIp, error));
            }

            var type = context.getString(OBJECT_TYPE);

            switch (type)
            {
                case "Server":

                    var server = context.getInteger(SERVER);

                    if (server != null && server != 0L)
                    {
                        sendServer(context.getString(OBJECT_IP), errorCode, error);
                    }
                    break;

                case "Network Switch":

                    var networkSwitch = context.getInteger(NETWORK_SWITCH);

                    if (networkSwitch != null && networkSwitch != 0L)
                    {
                        sendNetworkSwitch(context.getString(OBJECT_IP), errorCode, error);
                    }

                    break;

                case "Network Router":

                    var networkRouter = context.getInteger(NETWORK_ROUTER);

                    if (networkRouter != null && networkRouter != 0L)
                    {
                        sendNetworkRouter(context.getString(OBJECT_IP), errorCode, error);
                    }

                    break;

                case "Storage Device":

                    var storageDevice = context.getInteger(STORAGE_DEVICE);

                    if (storageDevice != null && storageDevice != 0L)
                    {
                        sendStorageDevice(context.getString(OBJECT_IP), errorCode, error);
                    }

                    break;

                default:

                    break;
            }

            //remove the item after processing...
            contexts.remove(targetIp);
        }
    }
}
